{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Discovered while fixing dbca-97ac-ad96-4d6d (potential-powellite-mouflon). This ticket is now **scoped to the one reachable, unambiguous site**; the two design-decision siblings were split out (see \"Split-out siblings\" below), following the /rebar-debug escalate-design-decisions guard.\n\n## Problem (in scope)\n`src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py:541` raises a **bare** `WorkflowError(\"unknown scripted step {name!r} (not in the step registry)\")`. Because `WorkflowError` subclasses `LLMError`, `error_code_for` (`src/rebar/_errors.py`, branch 7) maps it to `llm_unavailable`. An unknown scripted `uses:` step is a caller/plan-authoring fault, not an LLM outage.\n\n## Mechanism / reachability (proven — see Phase-1 RCA + CORRECTION comments)\n- The linter (`lint_refs.py`) validates step shape/fields but NOT scripted-step registry membership, so an unknown `uses:` name passes lint and is only caught at execute time by this raise.\n- **CORRECTED (latency finding):** the raise is caught by the interpreter (`interpreter.py:509-511` `except Exception` around `_dispatch`) and folded into a failed `StepResult` string — the exception TYPE is discarded. A runtime oracle (instrumented `error_code_for` + a real `run_workflow` with an unknown `uses:`) confirmed `error_code_for` is **never** invoked during the run. So the misclassification is a **latent** static property of `error_code_for`, with no observable `llm_unavailable` on any live surface today. The fix is a contract-completeness correction of the classifier (defense-in-depth), matching exactly how dbca handled the sibling subtypes.\n\n## Contract violated\ndbca established the per-subclass taxonomy: a workflow that WAS found but is invalid (parse/lint/migrate) is caller `invalid_input`; only the bare execute base stays `llm_unavailable` (protects genuine execute-time outages, dbca AC3). An unknown `uses:` step is a found-but-invalid workflow — the same class as `WorkflowValidationError`→`invalid_input`. dbca's own suite asserts `error_code_for(...)` directly for these subtypes, so classifier correctness is a directly-testable project contract. `invalid_input` is already in `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (no new vocabulary).\n\n## Fix plan (IMPLEMENTED — landed as Gerrit change 2395, merged f854924b1bc4)\n1. `src/rebar/llm/errors.py`: add `WorkflowUnknownStepError(WorkflowError)` — message passthrough, mirroring `WorkflowNotFoundError`.\n2. `src/rebar/_errors.py`: add `WorkflowUnknownStepError` to the `invalid_input` group in `_workflow_caller_code` (extends the existing isinstance tuple — no new branch, no complexity increase). Docstrings updated.\n3. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py`: raise `WorkflowUnknownStepError(...)` instead of the bare base, message preserved; import it.\n4. Held-out regression `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_workflow_error_codes_35ab.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] AC1: An unknown scripted `uses:` step (executor.py:541) classifies as `invalid_input`, not `llm_unavailable`, via `error_code_for` and the `_structured_llm_failure` LLM-tier surface. — Evidence: `test_unknown_step_error_classifies_as_invalid_input`, `test_unknown_step_error_structured_llm_failure_is_invalid_input`, and the white-box `test_dispatch_unknown_step_raises_unknown_step_error` (the raise site now raises the subtype). All GREEN.\n- [x] AC2: The bare `WorkflowError` execute base and genuine LLM outages (`LLMUnavailableError`, `LLMError`) still classify as `llm_unavailable` (dbca AC3 preserved). — Evidence: `test_execute_base_and_outages_still_llm_unavailable` GREEN; full dbca suite still passes.\n- [x] AC3: The emitted code is a member of `rebar.KNOWN_ERROR_CODES`; no new vocabulary added. — Evidence: tests assert `code in rebar.KNOWN_ERROR_CODES`; `invalid_input` already existed.\n- [x] AC4: Held-out RED→GREEN regression test asserts on the error CODE (not message text) and had teeth (mutation returns it to RED). — Evidence: RED first (missing type), GREEN after fix; two sandboxed mutations (revert raise site → `WorkflowError`; drop from invalid_input tuple) each returned the oracle to RED (`invalid_input`→`llm_unavailable` observed).\n\n## Split-out siblings (escalated design decisions — NOT in this ticket)\n- **551b-1a30-ac2b-4127** (sanidine-cilium-eland): editor.py:475 missing-bundle `WorkflowError`. CLI-only (not MCP-exposed; the CLI prints the raw message and never classifies), so not observably misclassified; correct code needs a NEW-vocabulary design decision the operator directed to escalate.\n- **73d8-4871-1b49-4047** (brainy-convulsant-unicorn): `ExpressionError` (execute-time workflow wiring) also classifies as `llm_unavailable`; whether to reclassify an execute-time expression fault is a design decision.\n\nOrigin: caused_by 8a31-e1c3-cf31-4239 (blanket LLMError→llm_unavailable), class plan_defect — same as dbca."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788048666290624133,"uuid":"0528e9ce-7e4f-436a-9d5d-dea3770afdea"}